# Pull Request

## 📖 Description

This PR adds a `deepMerge` utility function to update deeply nested state objects. This mutates the target object directly, updating keyed values and replacing array values.

### 🎫 Issues

Related to #7192.

## 👩‍💻 Reviewer Notes

Example usage:

```ts
const data = {
    prop: "hello",
    obj: {
        nested: {
            value: "test"
        }
    },
    arr: ["a", "b", "c"]
};

deepMerge(data, {
    prop: "world",
    obj: {
        nested: 42
    },
    arr: [undefined, "b", "c"]
});
```

Results in:

```ts
{
    prop: "world",
    obj: {
        value: "test",
        nested: 42,
    },
    arr: [undefined, "b", "c"]
}
```

