The `refresh()` method was attempting to trigger a re-fetch by calling `setData(null as any)` followed by `setPage((p) => p)`, but this doesn't change the `useAsync` dependencies, so no re-fetch occurs.

### Changes

- Introduced `refreshCounter` state that increments on refresh
- Added `refreshCounter` to `fetchFn` dependencies to trigger effect re-run
- Removed unused `setData` from `useAsync` destructuring

```tsx
// Before: No-op that doesn't change dependencies
refresh: () => {
  setData(null as any);
  setPage((p) => p);
}

// After: Increments counter, triggering fetchFn recreation
refresh: () => {
  setRefreshCounter((c) => c + 1);
}
```

